\title{Existential quantifier (#{\exists})}
\date{2026-02-04T14:46:11Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Next, we consider the \em{existential} quantifier, which lets us encode \em{existential} statements using words like "some" or "exists".  An existential statement is more specific than a universal statement: rather than saying that a proposition is true for \em{every} member of some domain, it just says that it is true for \em{some} members.}

